WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:09.092
A NETFLIX SERIES

00:47.964 --> 00:50.675
You want to live together with me?

00:51.259 --> 00:52.218
Yes.

00:52.302 --> 00:53.970
I want to be with you.

00:55.847 --> 00:57.599
Move in with me.

01:04.355 --> 01:05.982
Can I ask you…

01:07.025 --> 01:08.193
why?

01:11.071 --> 01:14.616
The cancellation fee for the wedding hall,
invitations, and return gifts

01:14.699 --> 01:17.494
will be paid with the honeymoon fund.

01:20.497 --> 01:22.165
We dated for ten years,

01:22.874 --> 01:24.292
but I still don't know you.

01:28.379 --> 01:29.798
I just feel empty.

01:30.381 --> 01:33.051
Ten years is never a short time.

01:33.927 --> 01:35.929
What was I to you?

01:36.012 --> 01:37.847
And what were you to me?

01:47.023 --> 01:49.400
We weren't right for each other.

01:51.528 --> 01:54.781
I'm relieved to have
at least found out now.

01:57.325 --> 01:58.660
So…

01:58.743 --> 02:02.122
it took us ten years to realize that.

02:09.420 --> 02:12.173
So I don't want to waste time with you.

02:14.384 --> 02:15.969
I want to get to know you,

02:16.553 --> 02:19.848
and I want to see
if we're right for each other.

02:20.723 --> 02:24.269
That way I can decide whether
to continue this relationship or not.

02:24.853 --> 02:26.396
That's why you want to live with me?

02:26.479 --> 02:27.522
Yes.

02:28.273 --> 02:31.860
We need to keep it a secret,
so we have to be careful at work.

02:31.943 --> 02:33.653
Wouldn't it be more efficient

02:33.736 --> 02:36.364
to get to know each other
if we lived together?

02:37.073 --> 02:39.701
If that's the reason,

02:39.784 --> 02:41.953
I don't recommend it.

02:44.747 --> 02:46.040
What do you not recommend?

02:46.124 --> 02:47.584
Living together.

02:48.960 --> 02:49.919
Why not?

02:50.003 --> 02:54.507
First of all, it doesn't make sense
to consider efficiency while dating.

02:54.591 --> 02:57.802
And living together doesn't mean
you get to know each other better.

02:58.344 --> 03:00.805
You have to make an effort to get along.

03:01.639 --> 03:03.308
So if that's your reason,

03:03.391 --> 03:05.602
I don't want to live with you.

03:07.020 --> 03:08.563
Hey, how do you know--

03:08.646 --> 03:11.024
I know because I've done it before.

03:18.197 --> 03:21.242
There must be a reason.
Why do you want to break up with me?

03:21.868 --> 03:23.828
- I'm tired.
- Of what?

03:23.912 --> 03:25.163
Of living like this.

03:25.246 --> 03:26.664
You wanted to live like this.

03:26.748 --> 03:29.459
- That's why we started to live together.
- Right, we did.

03:30.543 --> 03:31.920
But I don't think this is right.

03:32.003 --> 03:34.923
If this is the extent
of the happiness we can dream of,

03:35.006 --> 03:36.716
I can't be with you anymore.

03:38.426 --> 03:39.469
I'm sorry.

04:00.573 --> 04:02.492
What do you mean?

04:03.493 --> 04:05.119
You want to push back
registering our marriage?

04:05.203 --> 04:06.120
Why?

04:06.955 --> 04:08.081
What for?

04:09.582 --> 04:11.042
I'm confused.

04:11.626 --> 04:12.752
What?

04:13.336 --> 04:14.754
Honestly…

04:14.837 --> 04:17.006
I thought I'd be happy if I married you.

04:18.383 --> 04:20.218
But now I'm not sure.

04:20.301 --> 04:22.971
We fight and get angry
with each other too often.

04:23.054 --> 04:25.974
You aren't the person I knew
before we got married.

04:26.599 --> 04:28.643
What was I like before?

04:28.726 --> 04:30.270
You were mature.

04:31.312 --> 04:33.273
You were smart, but not cocky.

04:33.356 --> 04:35.108
You were kind and thoughtful.

04:35.191 --> 04:37.944
Above all, you had
a strong sense of responsibility.

04:38.695 --> 04:39.570
And?

04:40.655 --> 04:41.614
Am I not like that anymore?

04:42.865 --> 04:45.159
You have no plan.

04:50.832 --> 04:51.958
Is this

04:52.041 --> 04:54.085
because of applying
for a housing lease loan?

04:56.671 --> 04:57.630
It is, isn't it?

05:01.467 --> 05:02.593
Let's say

05:02.677 --> 05:05.305
we register our marriage
and get a loan like you said.

05:05.388 --> 05:06.681
What next?

05:07.307 --> 05:10.935
House prices will go up
while we pay for the loan.

05:11.019 --> 05:13.438
Then we'll have to get
another loan to lease a house.

05:13.521 --> 05:14.939
Do we have to keep living like that?

05:15.523 --> 05:17.775
We're still young.
What's there to worry about?

05:17.859 --> 05:19.986
We won't be young forever.

05:20.069 --> 05:22.447
It'll take us ten years to repay the loan.

05:22.530 --> 05:24.574
Even if we win the housing lottery,

05:24.657 --> 05:28.036
it'll take us about 20 years
to pay for it and make it ours.

05:28.119 --> 05:30.330
By then, we'll be looking at retirement.

05:30.413 --> 05:33.583
I don't want to work nine to six
until I'm that old.

05:33.666 --> 05:35.710
That's how everyone lives, Yu-jin.

05:35.793 --> 05:37.545
I thought we'd be different.

05:41.841 --> 05:45.303
We had a hard time getting married,
so we have to be different.

05:46.095 --> 05:48.056
We should be stable at least.

05:48.139 --> 05:49.682
Why are we so insecure?

05:52.268 --> 05:55.938
What did you think marriage was?

05:58.858 --> 05:59.901
I don't know.

06:01.277 --> 06:03.154
So until I find out,

06:03.237 --> 06:05.198
let's postpone our marriage registration.

06:18.503 --> 06:20.338
I wanted us to be close.

06:20.922 --> 06:24.592
I may have wanted to make up
for my failed past relationship

06:25.176 --> 06:29.013
by being close to each other
as soon as possible.

06:29.764 --> 06:32.308
You said you didn't want to get hurt.

06:34.185 --> 06:35.353
I don't want to.

06:36.229 --> 06:37.563
I feel the same way.

06:38.689 --> 06:40.274
But he says that

06:40.358 --> 06:44.403
the closer we are,
the more disappointed we'll be.

06:44.487 --> 06:46.572
And that the wounds
we'll inflict on each other

06:47.406 --> 06:49.450
will be deeper and more painful.

06:50.785 --> 06:52.120
We want to be close,

06:52.703 --> 06:54.914
but we're afraid of getting hurt.

06:57.542 --> 07:01.546
What is the optimal distance between us?

07:01.629 --> 07:06.759
EPISODE 7
OZONE WARNING

07:11.264 --> 07:12.306
Well…

07:13.683 --> 07:15.101
It's very small.

07:15.184 --> 07:17.103
With your budget,

07:17.186 --> 07:19.355
it's hard to find even a room like this.

07:19.439 --> 07:22.525
There are people lined up
for this room too.

07:22.608 --> 07:24.110
Can I see a few more places?

07:24.193 --> 07:26.904
Why don't you spend
a little more on monthly rent?

07:26.988 --> 07:30.658
Then you'll be able to find
a much better place.

07:33.161 --> 07:35.079
Please call me
if a new room becomes available.

07:35.663 --> 07:37.081
Sure.

07:37.707 --> 07:38.958
Thank you.

08:12.450 --> 08:18.372
MOTEL

08:25.588 --> 08:27.632
Stay here. I'll be right back.

08:29.342 --> 08:30.384
Did you buy mine too?

08:31.594 --> 08:32.553
Enjoy your ice cream.

08:32.637 --> 08:33.679
MOTEL

09:05.962 --> 09:06.796
Call.

09:07.463 --> 09:09.340
- What?
- Keep it at 50,000.

09:09.423 --> 09:11.175
- It's too early in the game.
- Hurry up.

09:11.259 --> 09:12.677
Okay. I got it.

09:14.011 --> 09:15.304
- All right.
- Ready.

09:15.388 --> 09:17.765
Then 50,000 more.

09:17.848 --> 09:20.268
Two packs of cigarettes? Okay.

09:20.351 --> 09:21.852
- Call.
- Call.

09:21.936 --> 09:23.229
- All right.
- Okay.

09:23.312 --> 09:24.522
- Show your hands.
- Who's the winner?

09:24.605 --> 09:25.940
- All right.
- What do you have?

09:26.023 --> 09:27.650
- Show it.
- Here it is.

09:27.733 --> 09:28.818
Five!

09:28.901 --> 09:30.820
- Your five is worthless. I have nine!
- What?

09:30.903 --> 09:32.238
- Come on.
- No!

09:32.321 --> 09:33.990
- Hey, I have 38!
- I got it!

09:34.073 --> 09:35.241
- That's weird.
- Seriously.

09:35.324 --> 09:36.367
- Why do you keep getting 38?
- Hey.

09:36.450 --> 09:37.910
- Be quiet and deal.
- Okay. Let me have a drink.

09:37.994 --> 09:40.371
- Seriously?
- Come on.

09:40.454 --> 09:42.456
- Hurry up. What are you doing?
- Quickly.

09:42.540 --> 09:43.541
Come on.

10:02.435 --> 10:05.688
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

10:57.114 --> 10:58.824
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

11:37.988 --> 11:40.366
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

12:30.583 --> 12:33.377
I'm sorry, but may I use your shampoo?

12:34.753 --> 12:36.172
Thank you.

12:41.844 --> 12:44.597
MALE SHOWER ROOM

13:03.407 --> 13:05.868
NIGHT-DUTY ROOM

13:10.498 --> 13:12.750
Does he think this is his house or what?

13:14.793 --> 13:16.003
- Hello.
- Hello.

13:16.086 --> 13:19.673
The scorching sun proves
that it is summer indeed.

13:19.757 --> 13:24.011
The UV index
in most areas today will be very high.

13:24.094 --> 13:26.555
The concentration of ozone
will be high as well.

13:26.639 --> 13:29.141
Don't forget to apply sunscreen thoroughly

13:29.225 --> 13:30.726
- when going out.
- This is nice.

13:34.063 --> 13:35.981
Is this one not taken?

13:36.857 --> 13:37.983
What do you mean?

13:38.734 --> 13:39.860
Why do you want to stay here?

13:39.944 --> 13:41.779
What about you, Senior Forecaster Um?

13:42.363 --> 13:44.073
I have my reasons.

13:44.156 --> 13:46.116
I have my reasons too.

13:49.411 --> 13:52.164
Gosh, this is nice.

13:58.295 --> 13:59.797
I'm leaving.

14:00.589 --> 14:01.840
I'm coming.

14:01.924 --> 14:04.260
Hurry up. I'm really busy today.

14:04.343 --> 14:06.971
I have to go to the office
for training in the morning.

14:07.054 --> 14:08.597
Plus, I have to make three visits.

14:08.681 --> 14:09.807
Will you be home late?

14:09.890 --> 14:11.642
You can have dinner alone, right?

14:11.725 --> 14:14.228
- Rice is in the rice cooker.
- Side dishes are in the fridge.

14:14.311 --> 14:15.688
I can just eat them.

14:15.771 --> 14:18.148
You're all grown up.

14:23.654 --> 14:24.947
Is that Dad's?

14:25.531 --> 14:26.866
Why did he leave it here?

14:26.949 --> 14:29.201
He always does as he pleases.

14:29.285 --> 14:31.579
Why did he even come back
if he was going to leave?

14:36.292 --> 14:40.129
Your dad doesn't like to throw things out.

14:40.713 --> 14:43.591
He keeps all the old stuff like this,

14:43.674 --> 14:45.009
so it's hard to tidy up.

14:45.593 --> 14:46.844
Do it if you want to.

14:47.511 --> 14:48.429
What?

14:48.512 --> 14:49.805
Divorce.

14:50.514 --> 14:51.557
What?

14:51.640 --> 14:53.309
Don't worry about me.

14:56.103 --> 14:57.229
Bo-mi.

14:58.188 --> 15:00.024
How can you say that?

15:00.107 --> 15:01.317
Um Bo-mi.

15:05.112 --> 15:06.280
Bo-mi.

15:07.031 --> 15:09.491
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

15:11.201 --> 15:13.871
- You're here early.
- Why are you coming out of there?

15:14.496 --> 15:17.499
Well, I had to do something.

15:22.963 --> 15:24.173
What did you do yesterday?

15:24.757 --> 15:26.050
I had some stuff to do.

15:27.468 --> 15:28.427
Why do you ask?

15:29.011 --> 15:30.638
You didn't call,

15:30.721 --> 15:32.598
so I thought something happened.

15:34.350 --> 15:35.517
Did you wait for my call?

15:37.061 --> 15:39.146
- No.
- You did.

15:39.229 --> 15:41.148
No, I didn't.

15:50.032 --> 15:51.367
We're at work.

15:53.035 --> 15:54.453
You waited.

15:54.536 --> 15:56.163
I can tell.

15:58.082 --> 16:00.209
Forecaster Lee, you may not know this,

16:00.292 --> 16:02.962
but I'm famous in the KMA
for my poker face.

16:03.045 --> 16:04.213
Also…

16:04.296 --> 16:07.299
- I'm born-to-be-impregnable.
- Who says?

16:07.883 --> 16:08.884
Me.

16:09.468 --> 16:11.720
Your subjective
objectification is fantastic.

16:12.972 --> 16:14.431
You're being cheeky.

16:15.057 --> 16:17.393
That's a sign of intimacy.

16:18.060 --> 16:21.355
Why do a director and a forecaster
need to be intimate?

16:21.438 --> 16:23.482
- Because we're a little special.
- What--

16:23.565 --> 16:25.234
Good morning.

16:25.317 --> 16:27.111
- Good morning!
- Hello, Assistant Director Shin.

16:33.409 --> 16:34.368
Shall we?

16:38.288 --> 16:39.957
Good morning.

16:44.712 --> 16:46.630
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

16:48.590 --> 16:51.719
- Doors closing.
- Wait for me. Please.

16:54.972 --> 16:56.265
Thank you.

16:57.307 --> 16:58.517
Doors closing.

17:00.936 --> 17:04.273
I saw that Assistant Director Yun took
a leave of absence.

17:05.274 --> 17:07.776
When I was with
the Disaster Prevention Department,

17:07.860 --> 17:09.319
he was my predecessor.

17:09.403 --> 17:11.488
I see.

17:11.572 --> 17:13.699
He isn't unwell or anything, is he?

17:13.782 --> 17:15.159
No, he isn't.

17:15.242 --> 17:17.536
I said he could take a break
for a year to study.

17:18.537 --> 17:19.872
How will your family get by?

17:19.955 --> 17:21.373
I'll continue to make a living.

17:21.457 --> 17:23.125
Goodness.

17:23.208 --> 17:25.461
Didn't your younger kid
enter grade school this year?

17:25.544 --> 17:27.254
It'll be hard to make a living alone.

17:27.337 --> 17:30.132
How can you be married
if you can't rely on each other

17:30.215 --> 17:31.550
through tough times?

17:32.468 --> 17:33.844
Doors opening.

17:37.890 --> 17:39.141
Not getting off?

17:43.437 --> 17:44.688
Doors closing.

17:52.404 --> 17:53.363
Thank you.

17:54.114 --> 17:55.365
Here you go.

18:00.120 --> 18:02.247
What's going on?

18:02.831 --> 18:03.665
Actually…

18:04.541 --> 18:06.960
a friend of mine got married recently.

18:08.087 --> 18:09.171
I see.

18:11.590 --> 18:12.591
And?

18:12.674 --> 18:14.426
He thought she was the one,

18:14.510 --> 18:17.262
so he pushed ahead with the marriage
despite people telling him not to.

18:18.388 --> 18:20.808
- And?
- They had their wedding

18:20.891 --> 18:22.684
but they won't register the marriage.

18:23.811 --> 18:25.646
He won't or she won't?

18:25.729 --> 18:27.189
The wife won't.

18:27.272 --> 18:29.316
What's going through her mind?

18:29.399 --> 18:31.568
Well…

18:31.652 --> 18:33.403
it's understandable.

18:34.571 --> 18:36.115
It's understandable?

18:37.533 --> 18:40.953
Maybe she got married on an impulse.

18:41.453 --> 18:43.705
She may have come to her senses later

18:44.331 --> 18:46.291
when she had to register the marriage.

18:48.085 --> 18:49.211
I see.

18:49.878 --> 18:53.215
Do you think she regrets getting married?

18:53.298 --> 18:54.591
Or…

18:55.300 --> 18:57.261
maybe she's scared.

18:59.513 --> 19:02.516
The moment it becomes legal,

19:02.599 --> 19:04.601
it feels like the game is over.

19:04.685 --> 19:06.603
It feels like you're crossing

19:06.687 --> 19:08.939
the point of no return.

19:13.152 --> 19:15.696
I can't be sure,
but I think the wife feels insecure

19:15.779 --> 19:18.073
about the marriage.

19:19.032 --> 19:20.742
Have him instill some faith into her.

19:22.119 --> 19:24.163
They say the moment you have faith,

19:24.246 --> 19:25.956
you gain courage.

19:26.039 --> 19:28.000
The courage that helps you

19:28.083 --> 19:31.003
walk through even a thorny path
with your loved one.

19:43.932 --> 19:46.602
- How is the atmosphere?
- As the upper level trough

19:46.685 --> 19:48.812
slowly recedes toward the East Sea,

19:48.896 --> 19:52.399
the anticyclone
that dominates Korea will slow down.

19:52.482 --> 19:54.151
The solar radiation will increase.

19:55.110 --> 19:57.196
The ozone concentration will go up too.

19:57.905 --> 19:59.489
By noon,

19:59.573 --> 20:01.408
it may reach the warning stage.

20:01.992 --> 20:05.996
Gosh, we'll be getting
a lot of calls today.

20:06.705 --> 20:09.291
- Notify the Air Quality Forecast Center.
- Yes, ma'am.

20:10.459 --> 20:14.504
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

20:25.307 --> 20:26.391
Isn't it ironic?

20:26.475 --> 20:28.227
What? What is?

20:29.311 --> 20:30.395
The ozone.

20:31.230 --> 20:33.273
When it's far away in the stratosphere,

20:33.357 --> 20:35.234
it's so beneficial,

20:35.317 --> 20:38.278
but it's harmful when it's close
to the surface of the Earth.

20:40.239 --> 20:42.824
Because there's always
an optimal distance for everything.

20:43.575 --> 20:46.078
At least you can calculate
the optimal distance

20:46.161 --> 20:47.537
between ozone and humans.

20:48.288 --> 20:50.999
Some distances
are impossible to calculate.

20:51.583 --> 20:52.918
Like what? For example?

20:53.001 --> 20:55.420
The optimal distance between people.

20:57.547 --> 21:00.676
You can't know it
until you've dealt with the person.

21:02.344 --> 21:03.762
Hedgehogs are like that.

21:04.513 --> 21:06.348
They get pricked countless times

21:06.431 --> 21:09.351
to find a suitable distance
to stay together.

21:10.727 --> 21:12.813
It's a relationship

21:12.896 --> 21:15.065
where you can only get close
by getting hurt.

21:15.148 --> 21:16.149
Right.

21:17.734 --> 21:21.863
There are people who haven't found
an optimal distance for over ten years.

21:22.447 --> 21:23.282
Like me.

21:26.618 --> 21:28.203
So did you go home?

21:29.037 --> 21:30.038
No.

21:30.122 --> 21:32.124
Maybe I've been away for too long.

21:32.207 --> 21:34.084
Now I'm confused.

21:34.167 --> 21:38.046
What's the most comfortable distance
between me and my family?

21:38.130 --> 21:40.632
Sometimes I wonder

21:40.716 --> 21:43.760
if it's best to see each other
only once in a while.

21:44.261 --> 21:46.638
That sounds like a cowardly excuse.

21:47.180 --> 21:48.265
Does it?

21:55.397 --> 21:57.691
The chance of heavy rain
is low today, right?

21:59.192 --> 22:02.112
Yes. Because it's less than 20 percent.

22:02.821 --> 22:04.072
Okay. Got it.

22:05.115 --> 22:07.951
Today's atmospheric ozone concentration

22:08.035 --> 22:10.954
is expected to be over 0.3ppm per hour.

22:11.538 --> 22:14.124
Please cooperate with
the Air Quality Forecast Center

22:14.207 --> 22:16.877
when they ask you
to check solar radiation and cloud cover.

22:16.960 --> 22:19.338
If you receive an outside inquiry
regarding ozone,

22:19.421 --> 22:21.381
please respond kindly. That's all.

22:21.465 --> 22:22.716
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

22:25.177 --> 22:26.386
I can't do it.

22:26.470 --> 22:27.804
During summer disaster prevention period,

22:27.888 --> 22:30.015
responding to the media alone
is a lot of work.

22:30.599 --> 22:32.350
I'm already writing monthly columns.

22:32.434 --> 22:34.019
How can I write a feature too?

22:34.102 --> 22:37.689
I know. So I told him it'd be difficult.

22:38.231 --> 22:39.483
It looks like

22:39.566 --> 22:41.276
he'll pester Reporter Chae,

22:41.359 --> 22:42.944
your wife.

22:43.028 --> 22:44.112
Pardon?

22:44.196 --> 22:46.823
The editor-in-chief asked me directly

22:47.407 --> 22:50.368
if you were Reporter Chae's husband.

22:54.331 --> 22:56.208
Don't you get it?

22:58.960 --> 22:59.920
Pardon?

23:00.629 --> 23:01.880
A feature?

23:02.672 --> 23:04.841
Isn't your husband KMA's spokesperson?

23:05.467 --> 23:08.512
The one who's on TV
every time there's severe weather.

23:10.138 --> 23:11.306
Yes.

23:11.389 --> 23:12.933
He's a great writer.

23:13.517 --> 23:16.812
I read his column in the KMA monthly.
"The Two Faces of Ozone."

23:16.895 --> 23:19.064
Your husband wrote it, right?

23:20.857 --> 23:21.900
Yes.

23:21.983 --> 23:23.652
Then why don't you ask him

23:23.735 --> 23:26.238
to write a feature article on weather?

23:27.322 --> 23:30.075
- Okay?
- Well…

23:34.621 --> 23:37.124
KI-JUN

23:42.170 --> 23:44.131
KI-JUN

23:52.556 --> 23:54.141
Hi, Ki-jun. What's up?

23:54.224 --> 23:57.269
- Are you busy?
- Somewhat.

23:57.853 --> 24:00.188
What is it? Why did you call?

24:00.272 --> 24:02.566
Do I need a reason to call you?

24:02.649 --> 24:04.985
I just wanted to hear your voice.

24:06.444 --> 24:07.863
Is everything all right?

24:13.910 --> 24:17.372
Of course. Everything's fine.

24:17.455 --> 24:19.040
Is it?

24:20.458 --> 24:21.543
Okay.

24:22.252 --> 24:24.004
Go back to work. See you at home.

24:24.087 --> 24:26.256
Okay. Bye.

24:41.980 --> 24:43.690
This is Kim Soo-jin of Chief Team.

24:43.773 --> 24:44.900
Is this the KMA?

24:44.983 --> 24:48.361
How can you issue
an ozone warning all of a sudden?

24:48.445 --> 24:50.155
My kid is going on a picnic today.

24:50.238 --> 24:53.450
So I took a day off from work
and prepared a packed lunch.

24:53.533 --> 24:55.869
You should have issued it a day before.

24:55.952 --> 24:58.914
Ozone increases suddenly
due to exhaust emissions

24:58.997 --> 25:00.957
or harmful substances in the air.

25:01.041 --> 25:03.168
So a warning can only
be issued in real-time.

25:03.251 --> 25:06.546
For your information, ozone warnings
aren't issued by the KMA.

25:06.630 --> 25:08.381
Stop kidding me. Hey!

25:08.465 --> 25:11.384
The weather is perfectly fine.
What's with the ozone warning?

25:11.968 --> 25:13.511
They won't let trucks and vans

25:13.595 --> 25:15.764
enter the metropolitan area because of it.

25:15.847 --> 25:17.515
You better make it up for us!

25:17.599 --> 25:21.144
Excuse me, sir. Please calm down.

25:21.228 --> 25:24.105
Contact the Ministry of Environment
or the Road Traffic Authority

25:24.189 --> 25:27.067
because ozone warnings
aren't issued by the KMA.

25:27.150 --> 25:29.319
Isn't ozone a good thing?

25:29.402 --> 25:31.112
I heard it was good to have it.

25:31.196 --> 25:33.448
That's when it's in the stratosphere.

25:33.531 --> 25:36.493
If the amount of ozone
in the atmosphere increases, it's harmful.

25:36.576 --> 25:39.079
Oh, I see.

25:39.663 --> 25:42.791
By the way, how old are you?

25:43.375 --> 25:44.376
Are you married?

25:45.418 --> 25:46.670
I'm hanging up.

25:55.053 --> 25:57.138
I'll answer it. Go and have lunch.

25:57.222 --> 25:59.057
No, I'll take the call.

25:59.140 --> 26:00.475
You should eat first.

26:01.101 --> 26:02.477
I don't have an appetite.

26:04.104 --> 26:06.398
Yes, this is Kim Soo-jin of Chief Team.

26:08.066 --> 26:09.567
Yes.

26:09.651 --> 26:11.778
Ozone warnings aren't issued by the KMA.

26:11.861 --> 26:13.822
Hello, sir.

26:13.905 --> 26:15.323
- Hi.
- Hello.

26:15.407 --> 26:16.408
Hi.

26:17.117 --> 26:18.118
Where is Director Jin?

26:18.201 --> 26:21.162
She went to the Policy Division
for post-analysis.

26:21.246 --> 26:22.205
I see.

26:22.872 --> 26:25.375
- Go back to work.
- Okay.

26:26.459 --> 26:28.044
Get back to work.

26:29.462 --> 26:31.047
- Senior Forecaster Um.
- Yes, sir.

26:32.007 --> 26:34.092
Let's grab some coffee. Come.

26:43.768 --> 26:44.602
Sir.

26:44.686 --> 26:46.521
Please don't yell at me.

26:46.604 --> 26:49.190
What? Yell?

26:49.274 --> 26:51.526
Who's yelling at you?

26:51.609 --> 26:52.694
You are.

26:52.777 --> 26:54.821
You've been yelling at me all this time.

26:55.697 --> 26:57.574
What? Hey.

26:57.657 --> 27:00.702
Do you want to get fired?
Do you want to submit a written apology?

27:00.785 --> 27:03.621
How dare you talk back to me?

27:03.705 --> 27:06.958
Hey, my son is a high-ranking official.

27:07.042 --> 27:09.753
I can make him sack you right now.

27:09.836 --> 27:10.670
Do you understand?

27:11.588 --> 27:12.714
Listen, sir.

27:13.298 --> 27:14.883
Why don't you complain directly

27:14.966 --> 27:16.801
to your high-ranking official son?

27:16.885 --> 27:18.511
Don't call us.

27:19.554 --> 27:23.016
How many times do I have to tell you
that ozone warnings are issued

27:23.099 --> 27:26.019
by the Ministry of Environment
and not the KMA?

27:26.102 --> 27:29.522
Call them and swear at them, okay?

27:41.534 --> 27:42.911
Can we do that?

27:42.994 --> 27:44.329
Of course not.

27:44.913 --> 27:45.747
But…

27:47.123 --> 27:48.416
we're people too.

27:49.459 --> 27:52.837
We have the right to defend ourselves
from rude people like that.

27:52.921 --> 27:54.422
Still…

27:55.715 --> 27:56.674
It's okay.

27:56.758 --> 27:58.968
Don't worry, Ms. Kim.

27:59.052 --> 28:00.512
I'll handle the consequences.

28:25.370 --> 28:26.830
Forecaster Lee, where are you going?

28:27.455 --> 28:29.749
I have something to do.

28:30.458 --> 28:31.376
Bye.

28:39.759 --> 28:40.844
Pardon?

28:41.469 --> 28:42.971
The rent is 600,000 won?

28:44.264 --> 28:45.890
Maintenance fee is extra?

28:47.392 --> 28:49.060
Well…

28:49.644 --> 28:53.648
How about 500,000 a month
including the maintenance fee?

28:53.732 --> 28:55.191
I told you no.

28:55.692 --> 28:57.861
The room you saw yesterday
is what you can get with that.

28:57.944 --> 29:01.322
Could you please talk
to the landlord one more time?

29:01.406 --> 29:03.491
I'll keep the room clean,

29:03.575 --> 29:05.952
and I'm only going to sleep there.

29:06.035 --> 29:08.538
I know the landlord won't say yes.

29:09.414 --> 29:11.666
Please ask just one more time, ma'am.

29:11.750 --> 29:12.834
Thank you.

29:22.302 --> 29:25.722
Why do you act like
a widower at Headquarters?

29:26.264 --> 29:28.266
I'm not a widower.

29:28.349 --> 29:30.643
I have a wife and a daughter.

29:31.561 --> 29:32.562
Exactly.

29:33.188 --> 29:34.731
You have a home and a family.

29:34.814 --> 29:37.317
Why have you been sleeping here for days?

29:38.193 --> 29:40.111
Because it's an extreme weather period.

29:40.195 --> 29:43.531
I used to live in the KMA
during summer disaster prevention period.

29:43.615 --> 29:45.658
Why are you nagging at me?

29:45.742 --> 29:48.828
That's because we didn't have
the central server back then.

29:50.038 --> 29:54.042
Now we can monitor the conditions
in China and Japan live at home.

29:54.793 --> 29:55.877
Anyway…

29:56.377 --> 29:59.839
kids these days don't like you doing this.

29:59.923 --> 30:02.050
Who are these kids you're talking about?

30:02.550 --> 30:05.136
A lot of people use the night-duty room.

30:05.720 --> 30:08.640
I've been getting so many complaints

30:08.723 --> 30:11.851
because you made
the night-duty room your home.

30:13.186 --> 30:14.771
Jeez.

30:15.480 --> 30:17.148
Pack up and go home.

30:18.441 --> 30:21.569
Isn't that why you came here
despite the lower position?

30:22.153 --> 30:23.530
Why did you come here then?

30:23.613 --> 30:26.366
You should have just stayed
in Gangneung and bossed everyone around.

30:26.950 --> 30:29.994
People in Seoul are so unkind.

30:30.078 --> 30:32.956
Does your wife know
that you're living like a bum?

30:34.499 --> 30:36.668
She told me to do as I please.

30:41.297 --> 30:42.423
Okay. Do as you please.

30:44.342 --> 30:47.512
What's the point of being able
to smell the east wind

30:48.429 --> 30:50.431
when you can't even read your wife's mind?

30:51.015 --> 30:51.933
Throw this out.

30:57.730 --> 30:58.898
Well…

31:16.749 --> 31:20.086
Who handled the complaint calls
that came to the Chief Team today?

31:20.795 --> 31:22.046
I did.

31:23.756 --> 31:24.757
What's going on?

31:25.341 --> 31:27.302
The Forecast Bureau received a warning.

31:28.845 --> 31:31.681
Did you tell someone not to call the KMA

31:31.764 --> 31:34.350
because the ozone warning
wasn't under our jurisdiction?

31:36.603 --> 31:39.022
I know it's difficult
to deal with complaint calls,

31:39.105 --> 31:41.232
but you can't yell at them and hang up.

31:43.401 --> 31:45.403
Did you do that, Ms. Kim?

31:47.864 --> 31:49.240
It was me.

31:50.408 --> 31:52.827
You shouldn't cover up for her.

31:52.911 --> 31:54.287
I'm not covering up for her.

31:54.370 --> 31:55.914
I'm the one who took the call.

31:57.498 --> 31:58.583
Look.

31:58.666 --> 32:01.169
This is what happens
when you don't do your job right.

32:01.252 --> 32:03.630
Why does a senior member
have to cover up for you?

32:04.213 --> 32:07.091
I said I took the call,
Deputy Director Han.

32:07.175 --> 32:09.677
I took the call. I yelled at him,

32:09.761 --> 32:11.721
and I hung up on him. Okay?

32:14.933 --> 32:16.893
You should have been patient with him.

32:16.976 --> 32:18.144
How could I?

32:18.227 --> 32:19.854
He said he'd get us all fired.

32:19.938 --> 32:21.356
I couldn't stand it.

32:21.898 --> 32:24.484
That wasn't a complaint. It was a threat.

32:24.567 --> 32:27.570
We aren't their emotional trash can.

32:27.654 --> 32:30.198
Why do we have to listen to that garbage?

32:33.034 --> 32:34.202
All right.

32:35.078 --> 32:38.289
In any case,
please do your job right, Ms. Kim.

32:39.832 --> 32:42.919
Why did you have
Assistant Director Oh take the call?

32:43.002 --> 32:45.755
This is all because you didn't
do your job properly.

32:45.838 --> 32:46.839
Am I wrong?

32:46.923 --> 32:48.633
Excuse me, Deputy Director Han.

32:48.716 --> 32:50.301
He crossed the line.

32:52.553 --> 32:54.138
As soon as I picked up the phone,

32:54.222 --> 32:56.724
he asked me if I knew who his son was.

32:57.433 --> 32:58.851
Do you know what else?

32:58.935 --> 33:00.520
He talked down to me,

33:00.603 --> 33:02.772
and asked me how old I was
and if I was married.

33:02.855 --> 33:04.774
He said I was a rude cow.

33:10.863 --> 33:12.115
You know,

33:12.740 --> 33:15.159
I came to the KMA to forecast the weather.

33:15.243 --> 33:17.161
I didn't struggle to pass
the civil service exam

33:17.245 --> 33:19.330
to handle trivial calls like that.

33:25.420 --> 33:26.796
Don't cry…

33:26.879 --> 33:29.549
I'll submit an answer
to the Audit and Inspection Division

33:29.632 --> 33:31.175
according to the procedure.

33:31.259 --> 33:32.260
You can go now.

33:32.343 --> 33:34.429
Yes. Okay.

33:34.512 --> 33:35.972
Let's do that.

33:52.780 --> 33:54.198
Ms. Kim.

33:54.824 --> 33:55.742
Yes.

33:56.492 --> 33:58.995
We are here to do that kind of work.

34:03.082 --> 34:05.168
What do you mean, Director Jin?

34:07.170 --> 34:09.380
Listening to the complaints

34:09.964 --> 34:11.340
is uncomfortable.

34:12.341 --> 34:14.969
But did you know

34:15.053 --> 34:17.472
that there are so many people

34:18.056 --> 34:19.390
affected by an ozone warning?

34:23.144 --> 34:26.856
Truck drivers whose livelihoods are
at stake, kids who can't go out to play,

34:26.939 --> 34:29.400
and those who don't even know
what an ozone warning is.

34:30.193 --> 34:33.654
If we didn't receive complaint calls,

34:34.655 --> 34:36.157
would we have known…

34:38.284 --> 34:39.660
how our weather forecasts

34:39.744 --> 34:42.914
would affect whom, when,
and to what extent?

34:46.417 --> 34:50.338
The reason why we're here after
passing the difficult civil service exam

34:50.922 --> 34:53.382
is to serve the people and the citizens.

34:54.926 --> 35:00.515
So there isn't any work
that's trivial to us like you said.

35:00.598 --> 35:01.808
Do you understand?

35:15.613 --> 35:16.739
Are you okay?

35:19.408 --> 35:20.576
It's all right.

35:29.794 --> 35:33.631
I didn't struggle
to pass the civil service exam

35:33.714 --> 35:36.008
to take nasty complaint calls.

35:36.884 --> 35:39.512
Why do I have to
put up with people like these?

35:42.014 --> 35:45.893
Then what do you think we're here for?

35:48.062 --> 35:50.648
We're here to serve
the citizens, the people.

35:51.149 --> 35:53.818
Take responsibility
and do your best at work.

35:53.901 --> 35:55.486
That's why the taxpayers pay us.

35:55.987 --> 35:58.197
Do you think this is just
a secure source of income?

35:58.281 --> 35:59.407
It isn't.

35:59.490 --> 36:01.617
Look for another job
if that's what you want.

36:02.285 --> 36:04.328
Without a sense of responsibility or duty,

36:04.412 --> 36:06.038
you can never work here.

36:06.122 --> 36:07.081
Got it?

36:21.053 --> 36:22.221
She's come a long way.

36:25.641 --> 36:26.726
Cheer up.

36:26.809 --> 36:28.477
You got scolded because of me.

36:28.561 --> 36:30.229
I'm so sorry.

36:31.147 --> 36:33.024
I don't consider it a scolding.

36:33.816 --> 36:35.067
Actually…

36:35.151 --> 36:36.694
it made me come to my senses.

36:38.905 --> 36:41.490
I've been answering
complaint calls all day,

36:41.574 --> 36:44.368
and that made me question
what I was doing here.

36:44.952 --> 36:47.121
But after listening to Director Jin,

36:47.205 --> 36:48.664
it became clear to me.

36:48.748 --> 36:50.249
Did it?

36:50.750 --> 36:53.085
You're all grown up, Soo-jin.

36:54.378 --> 36:55.963
That's how you make progress.

36:56.047 --> 36:57.965
Ha-kyung wasn't born like that.

37:00.801 --> 37:02.303
Anyway, bye.

37:02.386 --> 37:03.930
- See you tomorrow.
- Goodbye.

37:04.013 --> 37:05.431
- Take care.
- Bye.

37:09.352 --> 37:12.021
Is he going to sleep
in the night-duty room again?

37:12.563 --> 37:14.065
He's been away for too long.

37:14.148 --> 37:16.525
Being home could be uncomfortable for him.

37:17.109 --> 37:18.486
Doors opening.

37:18.569 --> 37:19.654
Hello.

37:19.737 --> 37:20.988
- Hello.
- Hello.

37:22.949 --> 37:24.242
Aren't you coming?

37:24.325 --> 37:26.369
You go first. I'll take the next one.

37:27.119 --> 37:28.913
- See you tomorrow, Forecaster Lee.
- Bye.

37:28.996 --> 37:30.289
Doors closing.

37:32.083 --> 37:33.292
Doors opening.

37:36.295 --> 37:38.130
You can go first.

37:41.717 --> 37:43.052
Doors closing.

37:54.563 --> 37:55.940
Doors opening.

38:00.319 --> 38:01.737
You can go first.

38:01.821 --> 38:03.281
- Doors closing.
- Bye.

38:41.152 --> 38:42.570
What are you doing here?

38:42.653 --> 38:45.364
The elevator was full.
I was waiting for the next one.

38:48.034 --> 38:50.369
I'm hungry. Do you want to grab dinner?

38:52.872 --> 38:54.165
Frozen pork belly?

38:54.248 --> 38:55.333
Sure.

38:56.083 --> 38:57.460
CHILDREN'S BOOKS
BEST SELLERS AND NEW RELEASES

39:12.141 --> 39:14.185
Is this the one you're looking for?

39:14.268 --> 39:15.353
Yes, it is.

39:16.020 --> 39:17.313
Where was it?

39:17.396 --> 39:18.731
I couldn't find it.

39:18.814 --> 39:21.233
It was in the storage.

39:22.568 --> 39:23.694
In the storage?

39:24.195 --> 39:26.405
You can pay for it over there.

39:26.489 --> 39:27.490
Okay.

39:30.701 --> 39:33.579
CITY CROCODILE
BY JIN TAE-KYUNG

40:18.249 --> 40:20.835
- Would you like to see it?
- No. Go ahead.

40:26.674 --> 40:27.633
Aren't you…

40:31.762 --> 40:33.222
You recognized me.

40:34.473 --> 40:36.809
Yes, I'm the…

40:37.768 --> 40:39.311
The side dishes, right?

40:40.312 --> 40:41.313
The side dishes?

40:42.148 --> 40:44.024
You left your side dishes with me,

40:44.108 --> 40:45.484
apartment number 1201.

40:47.319 --> 40:48.946
Apartment number 1302?

40:51.991 --> 40:54.910
I told her about the side dishes ages ago.

40:58.080 --> 41:00.040
Why won't she pick up?

41:07.006 --> 41:09.842
Please tell your sister

41:09.925 --> 41:12.928
to pick it up by tomorrow
or I'll throw them all out.

41:14.054 --> 41:15.181
Wait.

41:16.307 --> 41:17.600
You can't just leave.

41:18.934 --> 41:19.977
Why not?

41:20.478 --> 41:23.481
The book you were reading, City Crocodile.

41:24.190 --> 41:28.486
Please tell me which part made you laugh.

41:28.569 --> 41:29.612
Oh.

41:30.654 --> 41:33.199
I didn't laugh because it was funny.

41:33.282 --> 41:34.492
Why did you laugh then?

41:35.409 --> 41:37.453
Crocodiles have no choice

41:37.536 --> 41:39.872
but to become handbags
to come to the city.

41:40.998 --> 41:44.585
Crocodiles are reptiles
that live in the water,

41:44.668 --> 41:46.212
so they can't live in the city.

41:46.295 --> 41:48.297
But it's titled City Crocodile.

41:49.298 --> 41:52.051
Can't that be considered artistic license?

41:53.636 --> 41:55.054
I bet

41:55.137 --> 41:56.847
the author of that book

41:56.931 --> 41:59.099
has never even googled crocodiles

41:59.183 --> 42:01.727
let alone done any research on them.

42:01.810 --> 42:02.937
I'm sure she has.

42:03.020 --> 42:04.355
If so, she should know that

42:04.438 --> 42:07.399
a crocodile's front toes
and hind toes are different.

42:08.526 --> 42:09.693
Hind toes?

42:10.277 --> 42:13.781
Crocodile's forefeet have five toes

42:13.864 --> 42:15.908
and the hind feet have four.

42:16.742 --> 42:18.577
But that book…

42:19.203 --> 42:20.287
Jeez.

42:22.081 --> 42:24.792
I know anyone can become
a writer these days,

42:25.584 --> 42:27.878
but this one has no basics down.

42:27.962 --> 42:29.922
I laughed because it was pathetic.

42:32.299 --> 42:34.176
I'm sorry I don't have the basics down.

42:34.260 --> 42:35.302
What?

42:40.266 --> 42:42.476
Hold on. Are you the…

43:00.995 --> 43:03.247
- This one's ready.
- Thanks.

43:22.474 --> 43:23.434
Who was it?

43:24.685 --> 43:25.644
It's nothing.

43:26.812 --> 43:28.063
Is it good?

43:36.697 --> 43:38.741
Was I too forward?

43:38.824 --> 43:39.867
About what?

43:42.661 --> 43:46.373
Was it too much
to ask you to live with me?

43:47.625 --> 43:50.586
No. I was happy
because you were honest with me.

43:50.669 --> 43:53.464
So I was able to tell you
how I felt candidly.

43:55.716 --> 43:59.678
Ever since we talked about that,
you've been awkward.

43:59.762 --> 44:02.598
I feel like you're keeping
a distance from me.

44:04.058 --> 44:07.144
I thought you wanted that distance.

44:07.227 --> 44:08.687
You wanted this to be a secret.

44:08.771 --> 44:11.607
I don't want any secrets
between us though.

44:13.817 --> 44:15.110
Is it because

44:15.694 --> 44:17.529
I didn't tell you who texted me?

44:18.989 --> 44:21.033
That too.

44:28.332 --> 44:29.583
Here.

44:32.378 --> 44:33.754
Realtor?

44:33.837 --> 44:35.673
Yes, it's the realtor.

44:35.756 --> 44:36.924
There's a room available.

44:37.007 --> 44:38.592
Why the realtor?

44:38.676 --> 44:40.678
I can't stay
at the training center forever.

44:42.971 --> 44:45.683
I knew it was hard
to find a room in Seoul,

44:45.766 --> 44:47.518
but it's harder than I thought.

44:48.102 --> 44:51.146
I went around all day yesterday,
but I couldn't find one.

44:52.064 --> 44:56.110
Is that why you said
you had stuff to do yesterday?

44:56.193 --> 44:57.194
Yes.

44:59.321 --> 45:02.074
Si-woo, I'm really curious.

45:02.157 --> 45:05.119
Why would you refuse to live with me

45:05.202 --> 45:07.329
and look for a room to rent?

45:08.330 --> 45:09.581
It's because

45:10.332 --> 45:13.794
I want to keep my relationship
separate from my living conditions.

45:18.799 --> 45:20.634
It isn't because of your pride, is it?

45:23.679 --> 45:26.849
If this is how you react,
I can't be honest with you.

45:28.267 --> 45:31.228
I'm not proud of my current situation,

45:31.854 --> 45:34.314
but I'm not ashamed of it either.

45:39.111 --> 45:41.029
Why are you looking at me like that?

45:42.114 --> 45:43.115
It's nothing.

45:49.872 --> 45:51.957
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

45:53.375 --> 45:55.294
Can I have a bottle of soju, please?

45:55.377 --> 45:56.462
Sure.

46:23.113 --> 46:25.866
- What are you up to?
- Seriously?

46:32.414 --> 46:33.332
Unbelievable.

46:35.876 --> 46:36.793
Damn it.

46:47.596 --> 46:48.889
What's all this?

46:50.516 --> 46:52.809
You didn't have dinner yet, right? Sit.

47:00.609 --> 47:01.818
Thanks.

47:02.569 --> 47:03.570
Sure.

47:20.712 --> 47:21.588
What's this?

47:21.672 --> 47:23.423
CREDIT LOANS
FOR FULL-TIME CIVIL SERVANTS

47:23.507 --> 47:25.884
Our key money deposit
can be settled with that.

47:25.968 --> 47:28.011
It's still a loan,

47:28.095 --> 47:30.597
but the interest rate is lower
than the one for newlyweds.

47:30.681 --> 47:32.099
So it's much better.

47:42.067 --> 47:45.237
I heard your editor-in-chief
wanted me to write a feature.

47:45.320 --> 47:46.488
How did you know?

47:47.155 --> 47:50.075
Why didn't you tell me about it?

47:51.159 --> 47:52.828
I know you're busy,

47:53.453 --> 47:56.582
so I didn't want to bother you
with more work.

47:57.708 --> 47:59.960
Tell him that I'll do it.

48:01.336 --> 48:02.170
Really?

48:02.254 --> 48:03.088
Yes.

48:03.589 --> 48:05.841
If I don't do it,

48:05.924 --> 48:07.926
your editor will harass you, won't he?

48:08.010 --> 48:10.178
They'll talk behind your back too.

48:10.929 --> 48:12.472
Will you have time for it?

48:13.181 --> 48:15.267
I'll make time to do it.

48:15.350 --> 48:17.060
Because it's for my wife.

48:18.228 --> 48:20.480
I'll tell him tomorrow that you'll do it.

48:21.064 --> 48:22.441
Go ahead. Tell him.

48:27.904 --> 48:29.573
How did you find out about this?

48:30.490 --> 48:32.159
You're really amazing.

48:35.370 --> 48:37.080
Have him instill some faith into her.

48:37.581 --> 48:39.750
They say the moment you have faith,

48:39.833 --> 48:41.543
you gain courage.

48:41.627 --> 48:43.587
The courage that helps you

48:43.670 --> 48:46.381
walk through even a thorny path
with your loved one.

48:54.848 --> 48:56.933
- Did you finish your homework?
- Yes.

48:58.143 --> 49:01.188
Let's look at exponent additions today.

49:01.980 --> 49:03.982
- Solve this one and this one first.
- Okay.

49:14.868 --> 49:18.580
What did you mean
by what you said earlier?

49:18.664 --> 49:19.665
What?

49:19.748 --> 49:22.000
You said I could divorce your dad.

49:22.084 --> 49:23.627
Why did you say that?

49:24.211 --> 49:25.253
Just because.

49:26.630 --> 49:29.549
You look more tired now than before.

49:30.342 --> 49:32.427
You don't have to live with him for me.

49:32.928 --> 49:35.055
I'd like to live with Dad too,

49:35.138 --> 49:36.890
but I prefer you to be happy.

49:38.433 --> 49:41.019
I don't hate living with your dad.

49:42.312 --> 49:45.023
Well, it's just that

49:45.899 --> 49:48.360
your dad and I need some time.

49:48.443 --> 49:51.488
Because we've been apart for a long time,

49:52.781 --> 49:54.991
we need time
to be close to each other again.

50:06.461 --> 50:08.296
Ma'am, I'm done.

50:09.923 --> 50:11.049
Ma'am?

50:11.133 --> 50:13.009
- Yes?
- Can you take a look at this?

50:13.802 --> 50:15.887
Yes. Let's see.

50:38.243 --> 50:39.494
Goodness.

50:45.876 --> 50:47.294
Well…

50:55.343 --> 50:56.803
FRIED CHICKEN

51:00.599 --> 51:02.392
- Here you go.
- Yes.

51:04.352 --> 51:06.313
Did you already have a drink?

51:06.396 --> 51:09.775
Yes, I had a drink with my girlfriend.

51:11.318 --> 51:14.529
Why did you come here
instead of going to her place?

51:15.822 --> 51:16.907
Just because.

51:17.616 --> 51:20.243
Actually, I was a little embarrassed.

51:20.911 --> 51:21.870
Why?

51:21.953 --> 51:23.497
Because…

51:23.580 --> 51:25.707
I don't have a penny to my name.

51:25.791 --> 51:27.459
So…

51:27.542 --> 51:31.213
I held on to my pride
and barely survived until now.

51:31.922 --> 51:34.549
But my cover was blown today.

51:43.725 --> 51:44.935
To tell the truth…

51:47.938 --> 51:49.731
after my dad passed away,

51:51.733 --> 51:54.736
my family was kicked out of our house.

51:57.656 --> 51:59.866
My mom, my sister, and I

52:00.826 --> 52:03.703
suddenly had no place to go.

52:04.955 --> 52:07.749
I was hungry and the night was cold.

52:08.500 --> 52:10.710
I didn't want to stay out all night,

52:11.378 --> 52:15.507
so I wanted to knock on every door
and ask people to let me in.

52:15.590 --> 52:18.718
So what did you do that night?

52:20.679 --> 52:22.264
We slept on the street.

52:24.516 --> 52:27.477
The next day,
my sister was sent to my uncle's,

52:28.436 --> 52:30.897
and I went to my aunt's house.

52:30.981 --> 52:32.107
My mom…

52:33.191 --> 52:34.734
worked at a restaurant.

52:35.485 --> 52:37.612
So we lived apart for a few years.

52:40.907 --> 52:44.744
That's why I know
what it's like to have no home.

52:45.328 --> 52:48.123
And how weary you are.

52:50.625 --> 52:53.712
I respect your desire to separate
your relationship from your private life.

52:56.548 --> 53:00.260
I also understand
that you want to protect your pride.

53:01.678 --> 53:03.388
But you know…

53:05.765 --> 53:08.435
there's no need to go out of your way
to pretend you're okay.

53:13.189 --> 53:14.608
Do you know what I mean?

53:19.613 --> 53:23.825
So she called your bluff.
That's embarrassing.

53:25.160 --> 53:27.829
Well, yes. She did.

53:27.913 --> 53:29.247
But now

53:30.165 --> 53:32.208
I feel at ease.

53:34.669 --> 53:36.588
Because at least

53:36.671 --> 53:39.925
I don't have to pretend
to be okay in front of her.

53:41.843 --> 53:45.805
Even if I get closer to her,
I don't think it'll hurt.

53:48.183 --> 53:49.225
Right.

53:49.309 --> 53:51.853
That's how you adjust
the distance between each other.

53:54.356 --> 53:57.317
"The distance between each other."

54:01.112 --> 54:02.989
Gosh, I'm full.

54:04.741 --> 54:06.743
Let's stop babbling and call it a night.

54:08.453 --> 54:09.287
Pardon?

54:10.163 --> 54:12.582
Aren't you going to sleep?
We have work tomorrow.

54:14.292 --> 54:16.127
May I sleep here?

54:16.211 --> 54:18.046
I have no right to tell you yes or no.

54:18.630 --> 54:20.674
You know what? I snore.

54:20.757 --> 54:23.426
That's no problem at all.

54:23.510 --> 54:24.761
Okay.

54:38.984 --> 54:40.068
Damn it.

54:43.071 --> 54:50.078
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

55:19.482 --> 55:23.028
I submitted the report regarding Ms. Kim
to the Audit Division yesterday.

55:23.111 --> 55:24.237
Right.

55:25.822 --> 55:26.948
This is for you.

55:28.408 --> 55:29.242
What's it for?

55:34.539 --> 55:37.751
Well, do you know
the editor-in-chief of Munmin Daily?

55:38.460 --> 55:41.212
I guess he liked my column,

55:41.296 --> 55:44.049
so he asked me
to write a feature in his paper.

55:44.132 --> 55:45.633
Regarding weather.

55:46.968 --> 55:47.886
And?

55:48.595 --> 55:51.306
I was wondering if you had time.

55:52.390 --> 55:54.559
Didn't I tell you it was the last time?

55:55.185 --> 55:56.603
Please help me just one more time.

55:56.686 --> 55:58.313
I already told him I'd do it.

55:58.897 --> 56:00.148
So what?

56:00.231 --> 56:02.942
Just read through it once.

56:03.026 --> 56:04.319
It'll be the last time.

56:04.402 --> 56:06.154
Please help me this one last time.

56:06.237 --> 56:07.614
Hey.

56:07.697 --> 56:09.908
Does your wife know about this?

56:09.991 --> 56:12.410
Come on. How could I tell her?

56:12.494 --> 56:14.079
No, because it's embarrassing.

56:14.162 --> 56:15.580
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

56:16.372 --> 56:17.415
Ha-kyung.

56:18.458 --> 56:19.667
We're friends.

56:20.418 --> 56:21.419
"Friends"?

56:21.503 --> 56:23.046
We were together for ten years.

56:23.129 --> 56:24.380
Our relationship failed,

56:24.464 --> 56:25.840
but aren't we still friends?

56:25.924 --> 56:27.592
We were together since college.

56:27.675 --> 56:29.302
Except for our relationship,

56:29.385 --> 56:30.929
I still have fond memories of us.

56:31.012 --> 56:33.181
- Don't you?
- No, I don't.

56:33.264 --> 56:35.183
I forgot the time I spent with you.

56:35.266 --> 56:36.893
It's gone from my memory.

56:37.477 --> 56:38.311
Ha-kyung.

56:38.895 --> 56:40.563
If you ask me for another favor,

56:40.647 --> 56:42.315
I'll tell your wife.

56:45.485 --> 56:47.946
Ha-kyung, how could you do this to me?

56:48.029 --> 56:49.364
Ha-kyung!

56:50.156 --> 56:51.574
Director Jin!

56:53.910 --> 56:55.286
What should I do?

56:55.787 --> 56:57.455
Oh, no…

56:58.706 --> 56:59.916
Darn it.

57:04.963 --> 57:07.006
Good morning. Good work last night.

57:07.632 --> 57:09.509
Director Jin, you're always energetic.

57:10.093 --> 57:10.927
Thank you.

57:11.010 --> 57:13.596
Don't just look after yourself.

57:13.680 --> 57:15.473
Look after your team too.

57:16.182 --> 57:17.517
My team?

57:18.101 --> 57:20.645
Haven't you heard that they're living
in the night-duty room?

57:20.728 --> 57:22.647
You're talking about Senior Forecaster Um.

57:22.730 --> 57:25.859
Please be understanding.
He has his reasons.

57:25.942 --> 57:27.861
Does your team own the night-duty room?

57:27.944 --> 57:30.572
If two of your
team members claim the beds,

57:30.655 --> 57:32.740
where will the night shifters sleep?

57:34.951 --> 57:37.287
Did you just say two of them?

57:41.958 --> 57:44.210
It's your job to manage your team.

57:44.294 --> 57:47.922
Director Choi wouldn't have
let his team members be that way.

57:49.674 --> 57:51.092
Lee Si-woo--

58:02.729 --> 58:04.898
Why on earth are you two doing this?

58:05.482 --> 58:07.400
You can go to a motel

58:07.484 --> 58:09.277
or a sauna.

58:09.360 --> 58:13.323
But I only need a few hours of sleep
before going to work.

58:15.200 --> 58:16.659
It's too hot to sleep at a…

58:21.039 --> 58:22.665
Why are you here?

58:22.749 --> 58:24.834
Didn't you say
you'd stay at the training center?

58:25.835 --> 58:27.170
Well…

58:27.253 --> 58:28.922
He got kicked out.

58:29.005 --> 58:30.215
It's been a few days.

58:31.716 --> 58:32.759
It's been a few days?

58:33.843 --> 58:36.095
Have you been living
in the night-duty room all this time?

58:36.679 --> 58:37.555
No.

58:37.639 --> 58:39.516
He's been there for two nights.

58:39.599 --> 58:40.850
He slept in his car before that.

58:42.393 --> 58:44.270
Why would you tell her that?

58:47.732 --> 58:49.150
Unbelievable.

58:50.193 --> 58:52.946
Anyway, we're really okay.

58:53.446 --> 58:55.949
We'll take care of ourselves,
so just ignore us.

58:56.032 --> 58:58.493
How could I ignore you?

58:58.576 --> 59:01.371
Everyone is complaining
to me about you two.

59:01.996 --> 59:03.706
They should talk to us.

59:03.790 --> 59:04.832
What did they say?

59:04.916 --> 59:06.751
"Manage your team properly."

59:06.834 --> 59:09.295
"How long will you leave them unattended?"

59:10.588 --> 59:11.756
I see.

59:22.433 --> 59:23.768
What should I do?

59:24.978 --> 59:27.063
Hey, Ki-jun.

59:28.648 --> 59:30.984
I heard you agreed
to write for Munmin Daily.

59:32.193 --> 59:34.320
Well, yes.

59:34.404 --> 59:36.114
I did.

59:36.781 --> 59:39.742
I guess your wife talked you into it.

59:40.618 --> 59:43.913
You told me you couldn't do it yesterday.

59:44.455 --> 59:46.874
But you said yes to your wife right away.

59:46.958 --> 59:50.336
Well, that's not exactly how it happened.

59:50.420 --> 59:53.715
You're so devoted to your wife.
I hope you do a great job.

59:54.215 --> 59:55.758
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

59:57.552 --> 59:58.553
You're amazing.

01:00:00.263 --> 01:00:02.432
- Good luck.
- You're the best.

01:00:02.515 --> 01:00:04.767
Let's do it!

01:00:11.399 --> 01:00:12.567
What should I do?

01:00:28.916 --> 01:00:30.835
Do I have to do this?

01:00:33.463 --> 01:00:35.590
Yes, I have to.

01:00:36.299 --> 01:00:38.092
Yes. I'll do it.

01:00:39.802 --> 01:00:41.554
Reporter Chae's writing improved

01:00:41.638 --> 01:00:43.473
after she got married.

01:00:44.682 --> 01:00:46.893
The title hits the point.

01:00:47.393 --> 01:00:49.812
Her husband works at the KMA.

01:00:50.605 --> 01:00:51.773
Rumor has it that

01:00:52.357 --> 01:00:55.234
she lived with someone from the KMA.

01:00:55.902 --> 01:00:59.197
Did she end up marrying that guy?

01:01:00.448 --> 01:01:02.200
I guess so.

01:01:04.369 --> 01:01:06.329
I heard her husband can write.

01:01:07.789 --> 01:01:11.376
- I see.
- Reporter Chae has everything.

01:01:11.459 --> 01:01:13.544
Living with someone
and getting married to him.

01:01:21.177 --> 01:01:26.432
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:01:29.102 --> 01:01:30.978
Forecaster Lee has no place to go,

01:01:31.062 --> 01:01:33.356
but Senior Forecaster Um
can go back to his house.

01:01:33.439 --> 01:01:34.774
Right.

01:01:34.857 --> 01:01:36.359
I can't let him stay at my place.

01:01:36.442 --> 01:01:38.236
Because you have two kids.

01:01:38.820 --> 01:01:39.904
Now I have three.

01:01:39.987 --> 01:01:41.698
My husband took a leave of absence.

01:01:41.781 --> 01:01:42.740
I see.

01:01:42.824 --> 01:01:43.991
Why don't you take him in?

01:01:44.575 --> 01:01:46.035
I'll get going now.

01:01:49.080 --> 01:01:50.415
Not a chance.

01:01:51.082 --> 01:01:53.501
He has mysophobia, so he'll never say yes.

01:01:53.584 --> 01:01:57.422
I feel bad about Director Jin.

01:01:58.506 --> 01:01:59.674
Me too.

01:02:05.096 --> 01:02:06.931
Gosh, this isn't dry yet.

01:02:09.392 --> 01:02:10.977
How is sleeping in a car?

01:02:11.060 --> 01:02:12.729
Apart from feeling stiff

01:02:12.812 --> 01:02:14.605
and getting bit by mosquitoes,

01:02:15.148 --> 01:02:16.607
it's not too bad.

01:02:17.150 --> 01:02:19.736
Mosquito bites are itchy.

01:02:45.636 --> 01:02:47.221
How can I sleep here?

01:03:25.426 --> 01:03:26.844
Why aren't you coming in?

01:03:27.428 --> 01:03:28.387
- Oh, right.
- Okay.

01:03:31.349 --> 01:03:34.268
Senior Forecaster Um can use
the study over there.

01:03:34.352 --> 01:03:35.603
Forecaster Lee can take the small room.

01:03:38.147 --> 01:03:39.982
Can we really stay here?

01:03:40.066 --> 01:03:41.359
It's not for free.

01:03:41.442 --> 01:03:44.612
You have to pay a third
of the monthly maintenance fee.

01:03:44.695 --> 01:03:46.447
A third of it?

01:03:47.198 --> 01:03:49.992
If you don't want to do that,
you can go home,

01:03:50.076 --> 01:03:51.744
and Forecaster Lee can find another place.

01:03:51.828 --> 01:03:54.622
Si-woo, don't you think
a motel would be better?

01:03:55.373 --> 01:03:57.333
What about a sauna nearby?

01:03:57.416 --> 01:03:59.794
It'd be more comfortable than this place.

01:03:59.877 --> 01:04:02.588
I know, right? We'll get going then.

01:04:02.672 --> 01:04:05.132
Do you think of me as a woman?

01:04:05.216 --> 01:04:06.592
What are you talking about?

01:04:06.676 --> 01:04:08.636
No way.

01:04:10.054 --> 01:04:11.931
Just stay then.

01:04:12.014 --> 01:04:15.268
Let's say the three brains
of Chief Team Two are staying together

01:04:15.351 --> 01:04:17.687
for the summer disaster prevention period.

01:04:17.770 --> 01:04:19.897
A brain? Me?

01:04:19.981 --> 01:04:22.066
I don't think he's a brain.

01:04:22.650 --> 01:04:24.569
What are you saying? Did you forget?

01:04:24.652 --> 01:04:27.363
I predicted hail
in the metropolitan area last March.

01:04:27.446 --> 01:04:29.282
That was a fluke.

01:04:29.365 --> 01:04:30.741
You were just lucky.

01:04:30.825 --> 01:04:32.743
I also caught the heavy rain signal.

01:04:33.327 --> 01:04:35.204
Hearing that makes me want to drink.

01:04:37.164 --> 01:04:38.875
Should I go get some beer?

01:04:39.500 --> 01:04:41.794
Can you buy some dried squid too?

01:04:41.878 --> 01:04:44.005
Okay. I'll be right back.

01:04:47.008 --> 01:04:47.925
Well…

01:04:48.759 --> 01:04:49.886
Where's the bathroom?

01:04:49.969 --> 01:04:51.512
It's over there.

01:04:52.096 --> 01:04:54.849
There's a bathroom in my room,
so you can use that one.

01:04:54.932 --> 01:04:56.225
Okay. Thanks.

01:04:58.853 --> 01:04:59.979
Hey…

01:05:00.730 --> 01:05:04.150
I'm sorry to cause such an inconvenience.

01:05:04.233 --> 01:05:06.694
I'll find a place to stay soon.

01:05:06.777 --> 01:05:07.653
Okay.

01:05:13.659 --> 01:05:15.620
Seriously.

01:05:23.502 --> 01:05:26.631
What will Senior Forecaster Um like?

01:06:19.308 --> 01:06:21.602
Oh! The side dishes.

01:06:33.406 --> 01:06:35.116
Did he forget the passcode?

01:06:37.868 --> 01:06:38.953
You're back early.

01:06:40.871 --> 01:06:41.998
Ha-kyung.

01:06:43.332 --> 01:06:44.792
What are you doing here?

01:06:45.376 --> 01:06:47.294
You're here as I expected.

01:06:47.878 --> 01:06:49.755
I came by just in case.

01:06:49.839 --> 01:06:52.758
I don't care what you expected.
What are you doing here?

01:06:52.842 --> 01:06:54.010
I just…

01:06:55.636 --> 01:06:58.139
- thought of you.
- What?

01:06:58.723 --> 01:07:00.391
Can I come in for a second?

01:07:00.474 --> 01:07:01.851
Are you crazy?

01:07:03.602 --> 01:07:04.895
How did you know

01:07:04.979 --> 01:07:06.731
that I was going crazy?

01:07:08.232 --> 01:07:10.860
I'm so tired. Can I please come in?

01:07:12.028 --> 01:07:14.321
Tell your wife about how tired you are.

01:07:14.405 --> 01:07:15.781
Get lost.

01:07:17.033 --> 01:07:20.536
I have something to say to you.
Please let me in.

01:07:20.619 --> 01:07:22.371
No, you can't come in.

01:07:22.455 --> 01:07:23.456
Who's out there?

01:07:25.499 --> 01:07:27.084
Is someone inside?

01:07:28.127 --> 01:07:29.837
It's none of your business. Go home.

01:07:29.920 --> 01:07:31.714
- Hey.
- I hear a man's voice.

01:07:32.381 --> 01:07:34.383
- Who is it?
- Hey!

01:07:40.431 --> 01:07:42.516
I think I'm really drunk.

01:07:43.559 --> 01:07:45.061
Why are you here at this hour?

01:07:46.020 --> 01:07:48.439
Hey, it really is Senior Forecaster Um.

01:07:52.777 --> 01:07:53.986
Director Jin?

01:07:55.029 --> 01:07:56.363
Assistant Director Shin?

01:07:56.447 --> 01:07:58.365
Hey, Assistant Director Shin.

01:07:58.449 --> 01:08:00.451
Why are you here, Senior Forecaster Um?

01:08:01.160 --> 01:08:03.746
Because Director Jin
asked me to stay with…

01:08:03.829 --> 01:08:06.415
- What?
- Why would she ask him to stay here?

01:08:09.919 --> 01:08:13.422
Is apartment number 1201 your place?

01:08:14.507 --> 01:08:15.758
Yes, it is.

01:08:15.841 --> 01:08:17.510
Why are you here?

01:08:17.593 --> 01:08:20.012
I'm apartment number 1302.
I live upstairs.

01:08:20.763 --> 01:08:21.680
Pardon?

01:08:22.306 --> 01:08:24.100
Are you neighbors?

01:08:25.142 --> 01:08:27.144
Hold on. What's going on?

01:08:27.228 --> 01:08:29.188
Wait a minute.

01:08:30.564 --> 01:08:31.899
Doors opening.

01:08:35.986 --> 01:08:37.905
Hey, Seok-ho.

01:08:41.534 --> 01:08:42.868
What?

01:08:45.830 --> 01:08:47.915
What's going on?

01:08:47.998 --> 01:08:49.500
That's what I want to ask.

01:08:52.378 --> 01:08:54.296
Ha-kyung, what's going on?

01:08:57.049 --> 01:09:00.636
Life is always
a series of unexpected events.

01:09:05.683 --> 01:09:07.977
What's with all these people?

01:09:08.060 --> 01:09:09.770
Be quiet. Come with me.

01:09:11.564 --> 01:09:14.942
- How many more times
- Ha-kyung.

01:09:15.025 --> 01:09:18.737
do we have to stab each other
to find the optimal distance between us?

01:09:44.013 --> 01:09:46.515
How dare you come here at this hour
and cause a scene? Why?

01:09:46.599 --> 01:09:48.100
I'm sorry, Ha-kyung.

01:09:49.643 --> 01:09:51.061
My dear Ha-kyung was…

01:09:51.145 --> 01:09:53.063
Get off me. Wake up.

01:09:53.147 --> 01:09:56.400
I'm truly sorry, Ha-kyung.

01:09:57.568 --> 01:10:01.822
I keep falling for Ha-kyung.
It's getting out of hand.

01:10:01.906 --> 01:10:04.700
Are there still things
that haven't been sorted out with him?

01:10:04.783 --> 01:10:05.826
How long will this last?

01:10:07.036 --> 01:10:10.664
Who do you think
Reporter Chae's ex-boyfriend was?

01:10:11.957 --> 01:10:13.500
This is all your fault!

01:10:15.628 --> 01:10:16.629
Damn it!

01:10:16.712 --> 01:10:17.796
Stop it, Lee Si-woo!

01:10:18.464 --> 01:10:23.385
Subtitle translation by: Soo-hyun Yang
